s picture says what  characteristics of slave life does this  image show does this depict slavery if  we were going to have a single picture  that depicted slavery it should be a  picture  that demonstrates terror and violence we  also asked Ellis what he thought about  the picture well I think one of the you  know as we go through the the struggles  and the injustice is that the slaves  went through I think the important thing  is not to do what was done in earlier  times and and make it sound like they  were better off here than they were back  in there this picture this picture  doesn't look so bad you know there's no  marks on anyone's body and this is  supposed to represent enslaved people I  think the point that's being made is the  fact this was not a true representation  of what slaves went there Indian  justices that they went through and and  I can't answer why that made it in that  textbook we have progressed in in the  past five years and ten years and 20  years and we still have more work to do  and I think this would be an example of  that the publisher of that Texas history  book houghton mifflin harcourt told CBS  News in a statement that it appreciates  in values dr. Kennedy's analysis of the  textbook and they are making intentional  changes to the content and future  editions sin gage the publisher of the  American Pageant said the author's work  strenuously to provide an accurate fair  an engrossing account of American  history and they are always striving to  improve they note the newest addition  makes corrections and includes  first-hand accounts from  african-americans of the time so  important to point out though that the  publishers can make these changes but  it's up to the states to adopt them and  you know it's funny because I talked to  a girl friend of mine her daughters in  high school she just got an A in her US  history class and I had told her about  this story and she said we have to teach  them it's up to the parents and I think 